      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-241960",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/cf/cf4084e65ba98fd177312ba69946953e55e8b1f1613942bcd19c3be67e971dd9.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the points $A$, $C$, and $D$ are colinear and $AB^(\u27f7)\u2225CE^(\u27f7)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $m\u2220BCD = m\u2220A + m\u2220B$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $AB^(\u27f7)\u2225CE^(\u27f7)$ | Given |\n| 2 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $m\u2220ECD\u2245m\u2220A$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 4 | $\u2220BCE\u2245\u2220B$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 5 | $m\u2220BCE\u2245m\u2220B$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 6 | $m\u2220BCD = m\u2220ECD + m\u2220BCE$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 7 | $m\u2220BCD = m\u2220A + m\u2220B$ | Substitution |"
    },
