      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242620",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/3f/3f35e005e7053075e7ca388c3ef2032c8355aad2586f8aba493d36a58423e564.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the points $B$, $C$, and $D$ are colinear.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $x = y + z$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | {{field-1}} | Interior angles of a triangle theorem |\n| 2 | $m\u2220BAC = z + m\u2220CAD$ | Angle addition postulate |\n| 3 | $y + m\u2220BAC + m\u2220C = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 4 | $y + z + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C = 180^{\u2218}$ | Substitution |\n| 5 | $180^{\u2218} = y + z + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C$ | Symmetric property of equality |\n| 6 | $x + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C = y + z + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C$ | Transitive property of equality |\n| 7 | $x = y + z$ | {{field-3}} |"
